.TH HOLBUILD 1 "" "holbuild" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
holbuild \- project-aware build tool for HOL4
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B holbuild
.RI [ "GLOBAL OPTIONS" ]
.RB [ build ]
.RI [ "BUILD OPTIONS" ]
.RI [ TARGET " ...]"
.br
.B holbuild
.RI [ "GLOBAL OPTIONS" ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.br
.B holbuild \-\-version
.br
.B holbuild \-\-help
.br
.B holbuild
.I COMMAND
.B \-\-help
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B holbuild
builds HOL4 projects.
A project describes its sources, HOL revision and dependencies in a
.I holproject.toml
(or
.IR holbuild.toml )
manifest.
holbuild builds or reuses the HOL toolchain the manifest declares,
keeps build outputs under
.IR .holbuild/ ,
and builds logical targets such as
.I MyTheory
without the user managing Holmake state.
.PP
Global options go before the command, or before the target list when the
default
.B build
command is used.
Options of a command follow its name.
This page lists every command and option;
the README in the holbuild repository covers the manifest format and the
behaviour behind them in more depth.
.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.RB [ build "] [" \fITARGET\fR ...]
Build the targets, or the project's default targets when there are none.
Independent work continues after a failure, and the failure and everything
skipped because of it are reported at the end.
See
.BR "BUILD OPTIONS" .
.TP
.B context \fR[\fB\-\-trknl\fR]
Show the resolved project context.
Resolves metadata but does not build the toolchain.
.B \-\-trknl
selects the tracing-kernel context.
.TP
.B repl \fR[\fB\-\-from \fITHEORY\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\-exec \fIURL\fR [\fB\-\-remote\-only\fR]] [\fIARG\fR ...]
Start the HOL REPL with the project's context.
.TP
.B run \fR[\fB\-\-from \fITHEORY\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\-exec \fIURL\fR [\fB\-\-remote\-only\fR]] [\fIARG\fR ...]
Run HOL with the project's context.
.IP
For both
.B repl
and
.BR run ,
extra arguments go to HOL, except holbuild's global options and
.BR \-h / \-\-help ,
which holbuild takes wherever they appear, and Poly/ML runtime options
(such as
.BR \-\-gcthreads ", " \-\-maxheap " and " \-H ),
which holbuild's own runtime consumes and which it rejects where it can
detect them (Linux).
holbuild itself passes
.B \-\-holstate
and
.B \-\-noconfig
to HOL.
Targets are built without proof steps, as heap targets are: no step timeout
applies, and theories built by
.B build \-\-skip\-proof\-steps
are reused.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-from " THEORY"
Start from the
.I deps_loaded
checkpoint of
.IR THEORY ,
with its ancestors loaded, and load
.I THEORY
on top when it is built for its current sources.
Without a current checkpoint, start from the
.B [run].heap
the manifest configures, or the HOL base state.
Does not build
.IR THEORY .
Without
.BR \-\-from ,
when
.I .sml
scripts are given,
.I THEORY
is inferred: of the project theories the scripts depend on, the one with the
most ancestors.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-exec " URL"
Build the manifest's
.B [run].loads
and any
.B \-\-from
or inferred theory as
.B build \-\-remote\-exec
does, on the coordinator's workers, then start HOL locally.
.TP
.B \-\-remote\-only
With
.BR \-\-remote\-exec ,
fail instead of building locally.
.RE
.TP
.BI execution\-plan " THEORY" : THEOREM
Print the proof-step execution plan for a theorem (or an explicit termination
proof).
If a theorem and a terminating definition have the same name, the theorem
takes precedence.
.TP
.B check \fITHEORY\fR[:\fITHEOREM\fR] ...
Build each theory if needed, read its restored Theory.dat metadata without
starting HOL, and check the tags and hypotheses
of its stored theorems, or of
.I THEOREM
alone.
Prints one line per theorem that depends on an oracle other than
.B DISK_THM
(\fBcheat\fR, for instance), per theorem with undischarged hypotheses, per axiom
declared in the theory or its ancestors outside HOL itself, and per use of a
kernel-bypass call
.RB ( Thm.disk_thm ,
.BR RunCall ,
\&...) in the sources the theory is built from outside HOL.
Exits non-zero if there are any findings; otherwise prints a clean line and
exits zero.
Selectors share one target build and are checked in order; findings do not stop
later checks, but an invalid selector or unreadable theory data aborts the command.
The build runs without proof steps or checkpoints, reuses theories built by
.BR "build \-\-skip\-proof\-steps" ,
and applies no step timeout.
Accepts
.B \-\-remote\-exec
.I URL
.RB [ \-\-remote\-only ].
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-fingerprint \fITHEORY\fR ...
Print instead one line per axiom, definition and theorem stored in the
selected theories and their ancestors (HOL's included), sorted and
deduplicated:
.RS
.IP
.nf
fingerprint<TAB>THEORY<TAB>KIND<TAB>NAME<TAB>FINGERPRINT<TAB>ORACLES
.fi
.RE
.IP
.I KIND
is
.BR axiom ,
.B definition
or
.BR theorem .
.I FINGERPRINT
is the SHA-256 of the statement's term structure, the same for
alpha-equivalent statements.
.I ORACLES
lists the oracles other than
.BR DISK_THM ,
comma-separated, or is
.BR \- .
A script computes the same fingerprint with
.B HolbuildFingerprint.thm
or
.BR HolbuildFingerprint.term .
.TP
.B \-\-with\-fingerprints \fITHEORY\fR[:\fITHEOREM\fR] ...
Check the selectors and also print the fingerprint lines of their theories,
in the same HOL session.
The exit status is the check's.
.RE
.TP
.B buildhol \fR[\fB\-\-trknl\fR]
Build or reuse the declared HOL tree and print its path.
A configured remote cache restores toolchains and publishes successful local
builds automatically.
A global
.B \-j
is passed to HOL's
.B bin/build
when the toolchain is built here.
.B \-\-trknl
selects the tracing kernel.
.TP
.BI heap " NAME " [ \-\-remote\-exec " URL " [ \-\-remote\-only ]]
Build a heap the manifest configures.
.TP
.BI executable " NAME " [ \-\-remote\-exec " URL " [ \-\-remote\-only ]]
Build an executable heap the manifest configures.
.TP
.BI clean " THEORY" ...
Remove local build outputs of theories.
A later build may restore the outputs from the global cache; to execute a
theory from the beginning, run
.B clean
and then
.BR "build \-\-force=theory" .
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB\-\-build\fR [\fB\-\-remote\-exec \fIURL\fR [\fB\-\-remote\-only\fR]]] [\fB\-\-closure\fR | \fB\-\-sources\-only\fR] \fB\-o \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-metadata\-out \fIFILE\fR] [\fITARGET\fR ...]
Write the root package as an hbx capsule: its source snapshot and the cached
build outputs of its own theories among the targets.
Targets in other packages are left out.
.RS
.TP
.B \-o \fIFILE\fR, \-\-output \fIFILE\fR
The archive to write.
.TP
.BI \-\-metadata\-out " FILE"
Also write the outputs' metadata to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-\-build
Build the targets first.
With
.BR \-\-remote\-exec ,
as
.B build
does.
.TP
.B \-\-closure
Write the cached outputs of the whole target closure, dependencies included,
and no source snapshot.
.TP
.B \-\-sources\-only
Write the source snapshot only.
Takes no targets and builds no theories.
.RE
.TP
.BI import " FILE"
Import the cached build outputs from an hbx archive into the global cache.
.TP
.B gc \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Remove stale project and cache state, including HOL toolchains unused for the
retention period.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-retention\-days " DAYS" "\fR, \fB\-\-days " DAYS
Retention period (default: 7).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-checkpoints\-gb " GB"
Size limit for the project's checkpoints, in GB (default: the
.B [build].checkpoint_limit_gb
of
.IR .holconfig.toml ,
or 5).
Applies only to project cleanup.
.TP
.B \-\-clean\-only
Project state only.
.TP
.B \-\-cache\-only
Global cache only; no project is needed.
.TP
.B \-\-toolchains\-only
Installed HOL toolchains only; no project is needed.
.RE
.IP
The three
.B \-\-*\-only
options are mutually exclusive.
.TP
.BI cache " gc"
Deprecated; use
.BR "gc \-\-cache\-only" .
Takes
.B \-\-retention\-days
and
.BR \-\-days .
.TP
.B action\-spec \fR[\fB\-\-upload\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITARGET\fR ...]
Plan the targets as
.B build
would and write the action specification of every theory the remote cache
cannot satisfy to
.IR .holbuild/action\-specs/SHA256 ,
then print the action batch.
Takes
.BR build 's
cache and proof options and
.BR \-\-tool\-cache .
Needs
.BR \-\-remote\-cache .
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-upload
Also upload the specs and their sources to the remote cache.
.RE
.TP
.B exec\-action \fISPEC\-SHA256\fR \fB\-\-cache\-limit\-gb \fIN\fR [\fB\-\-cache\-reserve\-gb \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-share\-heaps\fR] [\fB\-\-result \fIFILE\fR]
Run the action specification stored in the remote cache as
.I SPEC\-SHA256
(see
.BR action\-spec ),
or the run spec (see
.BR run\-action ),
as a remote worker would, and publish its result to the remote cache.
Needs
.BR \-\-remote\-cache .
The action runs in
.IR CACHE/action ,
with checkpoints in
.IR CACHE/checkpoints ,
where
.I CACHE
is the cache root.
Writes a
.I holbuild\-action\-result\-v1
record to
.IR FILE ,
or to standard output.
.IP
Exit status: 0 built or cached; 1 proof, tactic-timeout, script or timeout
failure; 2 out of memory; 3 input-missing, publish, toolchain, disk or
internal failure; 4 spec rejected.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-limit\-gb " N"
Before the action, evict least recently used checkpoints, toolchains and local
cache entries until the cache root holds at most
.I N
GB minus the reserve.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-reserve\-gb " N"
Room to keep free under the limit (default: a tenth).
.TP
.B \-\-share\-heaps
Resume from the deps-loaded heap and theorem checkpoints other workers
published, and publish this run's.
The host store
.I CACHE/checkpoint\-store
keeps their files.
.TP
.BI \-\-result " FILE"
Where to write the result record (default: standard output).
.RE
.TP
.B run\-action \fIFORM\fR \fITARGET\fR ...
Run script
.I S
in the context of each target on remote workers, once per set of inputs:
runs the remote cache already holds are not run again.
The others go to the coordinator as one batch; then every run's outputs are
fetched into
.IR D/PACKAGE/THEORY
.RI ( D/HOL/THEORY
for a toolchain theory), beside
.I KEY
(the run key) and
.IR CONTEXT .
Runs never execute locally.
For each run a line is printed:
.IR "CONTEXT RUN\-KEY" " done|cached|failed " "CLASS|missing" .
A target is a project theory (a logical name as
.B build
takes, or
.IR PACKAGE:NAME ),
a theory of the HOL toolchain
.RB ( hol:bool
or
.BR hol:boolTheory ),
or
.B hol:*
for every theory of the toolchain.
A project theory must be built, in the local or remote cache, first.
Takes
.BR build 's
cache options.
Needs
.BR \-\-remote\-cache .
.IP
There are three forms; a
.I \-\-script
is required in each:
.RS
.IP
.nf
run\-action \-\-remote\-exec URL [\-\-remote\-only] \-\-outputs\-dir D [\-\-profile P]
    \-\-script S [\-\-support F]... [\-\-load L]... \-\-output N...
    [\-\-option timeout=SECONDS] [\-\-closure] TARGET...
run\-action \-\-fetch\-only \-\-outputs\-dir D \-\-script S ... TARGET...
run\-action \-\-export\-only \-\-script S ... TARGET...
.fi
.RE
.IP
.B \-\-export\-only
takes none of
.BR \-\-fetch\-only ,
.BR \-\-remote\-exec ,
.BR \-\-remote\-only ,
.B \-\-outputs\-dir
and
.BR \-\-profile .
.IP
Exits 0 when every run ended (done, cached, failed or, with
.BR \-\-fetch\-only ,
missing), 75 when the coordinator cannot take or finish the batch or an
ended run cannot be fetched, and 1 on errors, a cancelled batch, or a target
that is not built.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-exec " URL"
The coordinator to submit to.
.TP
.B \-\-remote\-only
Exit 75, not 1, when no
.B \-\-remote\-exec
is given.
.TP
.BI \-\-outputs\-dir " D"
Where to fetch the outputs.
.TP
.BI \-\-script " S"
The script to run.
.TP
.BI \-\-support " F"
A file the script reads, under the script's directory.
May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-load " L"
A library to load before the script, in order.
May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " N"
A file the script writes.
At least one is required; may be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-option " timeout=SECONDS"
How long a run may take; not part of its key.
.TP
.B \-\-closure
Also run in the context of each project target's ancestry.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " P"
The coordinator's memory profile for the batch.
.TP
.B \-\-fetch\-only
Fetch what the remote cache holds; submit nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-export\-only
Only write and upload each run's spec, and print
.IR "CONTEXT RUN\-KEY SPEC\-SHA256" .
.RE
.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global options come before the command.
.TP
.BI \-\-source\-dir " PATH"
The project source directory.
Defaults to
.B HOLBUILD_SOURCE_DIR
or the current working directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-dir " PATH"
The global cache directory.
Overrides
.B HOLBUILD_CACHE
and the default,
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/holbuild
or, when that is unset,
.IR $HOME/.cache/holbuild .
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Disable holbuild-managed network access (Git, remote cache and coordinator).
Also enabled by
.BR HOLBUILD_OFFLINE=1 .
Explicit
.B \-\-remote\-cache
or
.B \-\-remote\-exec
conflicts with it.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-cache " URL"
Comma-separated Bazel-style HTTP remote cache endpoints.
Also configurable with
.B HOLBUILD_REMOTE_CACHE_URL
or the project's
.IR .holconfig.toml ;
the option overrides the environment variable.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit newline-delimited JSON where supported.
Several commands reject it.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR, \fB\-\-verbosity \fILEVEL
Adjust status output.
.I LEVEL
is one of
.BR quiet ,
.B normal
and
.BR verbose .
.TP
.B \-j \fIN\fR, \-j\fIN\fR, \-\-jobs \fIN
Build parallelism.
Without it, the
.B jobs
of the
.B [build]
table in
.I .holconfig.toml
applies, and otherwise half the detected processors (at least 1).
When holbuild builds a HOL toolchain it also passes
.BI \-j " N"
to HOL's
.BR bin/build ;
without it,
.B bin/build
uses HOL's own default.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-heap " MB"
Poly/ML maximum heap size for child HOL processes, including remote workers
(which use their configured default, 12000 MB, without it).
Do not use
.BR \-\-maxheap :
holbuild is itself a Poly/ML program, whose runtime takes
.B \-\-maxheap
as the cap on its own heap, so the option never reaches holbuild and the
children run uncapped.
holbuild rejects it where it can detect it (Linux).
.TP
.BI \-\-prefetch\-concurrency " N"
How many remote cache entries a build copies into the local cache at once,
ahead of the build workers; also limits remote-cache existence checks before
batch export.
Defaults to 50 or twice the number of jobs, whichever is larger.
Only used with a remote cache.
.TP
.BI \-\-cooperate\-dir " DIR"
Share a machine memory budget with every holbuild process using
.IR DIR .
Also settable with
.BR HOLBUILD_COOPERATE_DIR .
See
.BR "MEMORY ADMISSION" .
.TP
.BI \-\-machine\-max\-mem " MB"
The budget to record in
.I DIR/budget
when that file does not exist yet (default without it:
.B MemTotal
less a reserve).
A value that differs from the file at this process's first admission is an
error.
.TP
.BI \-\-child\-charge " MB"
What each child reserves against the budget.
Defaults to
.BR \-\-max\-heap ,
at most 3072 (3072 without
.BR \-\-max\-heap );
where
.B MemAvailable
cannot be read, to
.BR \-\-max\-heap " + 1024,"
and then
.B \-\-max\-heap
or
.B \-\-child\-charge
is required.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Print help.
With a command name, print that command's help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.
.SH BUILD OPTIONS
Options of
.BR build ,
placed after the word
.B build
or, when it is omitted, before the targets.
.TP
.B \-\-watch
Build, then watch the project inputs with
.B inotifywait
(from inotify-tools) and rebuild after changes.
Does not support
.BR \-\-json ,
.B \-\-dry\-run
or
.BR \-\-repl\-on\-failure .
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-fast
Stop after the first failure and cancel unfinished work.
The default is to finish independent work and skip only the dependents of
failures.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be built without building.
.TP
.BR \-\-force [=\fILEVEL\fR]
Bypass cached outputs.
.I LEVEL
is
.B theory
(the requested targets; also
.BR target ),
.B project
(every theory of the root package in the build plan) or
.B full
(every theory in the plan, dependencies included; also
.BR all );
a bare
.B \-\-force
means
.BR full .
Valid checkpoints, including failed proof prefixes, may still resume.
To execute a theory from the beginning while keeping cache hits for its
ancestors, run
.B holbuild clean
on it, then
.BR "build \-\-force=theory" .
.B \-\-force\-theory ,
.B \-\-force\-project
and
.B \-\-force\-full
are the same levels as separate flags.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Do not use the global or remote build cache.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-cache\-timeout\-discrepancy
Reuse cached theory artifacts even when their recorded proof timeout does not
satisfy the requested one.
Project metadata keeps the artifact's recorded timeout, so a later build
without the flag applies the strict check.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-stat\-cache
Hash every source file instead of trusting an unchanged file status.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-checkpoints
Do not create checkpoints.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-checkpoints
All root-package theories save checkpoints by default, except a theory that
is not a target and that a parallel build pipelines into an idle slot.
With this flag every such theory saves them.
Checkpoint policy does not change theory outputs or cache keys.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-proof\-steps
Do not execute proof steps (no per-step timeout, tracing or step
diagnostics).
.TP
.BR \-\-proof\-scope " \fIroot\fR|\fIall\fR (default: " root )
Which theories receive proof instrumentation and the invocation's timeout.
.B all
includes dependency theories in the selected build plan, and conflicts with
.BR \-\-skip\-proof\-steps .
Use
.B \-\-force=full \-\-no\-cache
for a full audit.
Also accepted as
.BR \-\-proof\-scope=\fIscope .
.TP
.BI \-\-tactic\-timeout " SECONDS"
Per-step timeout for proof steps;
.B 0
disables it.
Without the option, the
.B tactic_timeout
of the
.B [build]
table in
.I .holconfig.toml
or the manifest applies, and otherwise 2.5 seconds.
A step that times out runs once more with half the timeout; if that finishes,
the step passes, and otherwise it fails the build, even inside
.B TRY
or an
.B ORELSE
alternative.
Also accepted as
.BR \-\-tactic\-timeout=\fISECONDS .
.TP
.B \-\-trace\-steps
Execute and record proof-step traces for theories in the proof scope,
including up-to-date ones; skips checkpoint replay.
Not supported with
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B \-\-repl\-on\-failure
After a theory fails, start a HOL REPL from the newest useful checkpoint.
Serialises the build; not supported with
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B \-\-retain\-debug\-artifacts
Retain the durable failure logs of failed theories (reported as
.I debug_artifacts.log
in JSON mode, where failure evidence is otherwise bounded).
.TP
.B \-\-emit\-output\-hashes
Record output hashes for diagnostics.
.TP
.B \-\-warn\-unreachable
Report discoverable theory scripts that are outside the root dependency closure.
.TP
.B \-\-trknl
Use the tracing-kernel toolchain.
Needs a Poly/ML that provides the tracing-kernel export support; set
.B HOLBUILD_POLY
to it.
Tracing builds record the proof trace of each theory as
.IR Theory.tr.gz .
.TP
.BI \-\-tool\-cache " NAME"
Give each theory's HOL processes
.BR HOLBUILD_TOOL_CACHE_DIR ,
a directory a tool keeps files in from one build to the next:
.IR $HOLBUILD_CACHE/tool\-cache/ NAME
locally; on a remote worker, one the remote cache fills and saves per
theory dependencies.
.I NAME
is letters, digits,
.BR . ,
.B _
and
.BR \- .
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-exec " URL"
Build the theories the remote cache lacks, and that are not built here for
their current inputs (except with
.BR \-\-detach ),
on the coordinator's workers and restore them from the remote cache.
Needs
.BR \-\-remote\-cache .
A closure that cannot run remotely, or an unreachable coordinator, builds
locally.
.TP
.B \-\-remote\-only
With
.BR \-\-remote\-exec :
fail instead of building locally, with exit status 75.
.TP
.BI \-\-priority " N"
The batch's priority with the coordinator (default 0).
.TP
.B \-\-detach
Submit the batch and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-attach " BATCH\-ID"
Follow a submitted batch and restore it.
.
.SH DEPRECATED AND REMOVED OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-goalfrag
Deprecated; warns and behaves like
.BR \-\-skip\-proof\-steps .
.TP
.B \-\-goalfrag\-trace
Deprecated; warns and behaves like
.BR \-\-trace\-steps .
.TP
.B \-\-new\-ir
Deprecated; accepted and ignored.
.TP
.BR \-\-goalfrag ", " \-\-goalfrag\-plan
Removed: proof steps are on by default, and
.B execution\-plan
replaces the plan flag.
.TP
.B \-\-holdir
Removed: the HOL used is the manifest's
.BR [dependencies.hol] .
.
.SH MEMORY ADMISSION
Independent holbuild processes on one machine can share a memory budget with
.BR \-\-cooperate\-dir .
Each theory, generator or heap-export child reserves
.BR \-\-child\-charge ,
and starts only while all reservations in
.I DIR
plus its own fit the budget and, while other children hold reservations,
.B MemAvailable
less the charges of children started in the last 30 seconds covers its charge
plus a margin.
The reserve is a quarter of
.BR MemTotal ,
at least 1 GiB and at most 30 GiB; the margin is the reserve, or what the budget
leaves out of
.B MemTotal
if that is less (at least 1 GiB).
This bounds admission; it does not enforce resident size.
HOL toolchain builds,
.BR check ,
.B run
and
.B repl
reserve nothing.
.PP
The budget is the byte count in
.IR DIR/budget .
To set or resize it, write the file while holding
.IR DIR/lock :
.IP
.nf
flock DIR/lock sh \-c 'echo BYTES > DIR/budget.new && mv DIR/budget.new DIR/budget'
.fi
.PP
To return to the default, remove it:
.BR "flock DIR/lock rm DIR/budget" .
Waiting for
.I DIR/lock
gives up after
.B HOLBUILD_COOPERATE_LOCK_TIMEOUT
seconds.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_CACHE
The global cache directory (overridden by
.BR \-\-cache\-dir ).
Without it, the default is
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/holbuild
or, when
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
is unset,
.IR $HOME/.cache/holbuild .
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_SOURCE_DIR
The project source directory (overridden by
.BR \-\-source\-dir ).
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_OFFLINE
.B 1
enables
.BR \-\-offline ;
.B 0
leaves online behaviour unchanged.
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_REMOTE_CACHE_URL
Remote cache endpoints (overridden by
.BR \-\-remote\-cache ).
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_REMOTE_CACHE_CURL_CONFIG
A curl configuration file for remote cache requests; overrides the
.I .holconfig.toml
setting.
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_REMOTE_EXEC_CURL_CONFIG
A curl configuration file for requests to the remote-execution coordinator.
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_COOPERATE_DIR
As
.BR \-\-cooperate\-dir .
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_COOPERATE_LOCK_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait for the memory-budget lock before failing (default 600;
.B 0
waits without limit).
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_POLY
The
.B poly
executable used to build or run project HOL toolchains, for example a
tracing-kernel Poly/ML for
.BR \-\-trknl .
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_POLYC
The
.B polyc
executable used to build HOL toolchains (default
.BR polyc ).
.TP
.BR HOLDIR ", " HOLBUILD_HOLDIR
Ignored by project builds, which use the manifest's
.BR [dependencies.hol] .
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_PIPELINE
.B off
turns off pipelining of non-target cold theories into idle job slots.
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_PLAN_RECORD
.B off
turns off the plan record;
.B check
also plans in full and fails the build if the two plans differ.
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_PROOF_THREADS
Number of threads for checking a theory's proofs (default: up to 4 of the
build's jobs).
.TP
.BR HOLBUILD_FAILED_GOALS_LIMIT ", " HOLBUILD_GOAL_STATE_LIMIT
Byte limits for the all-input-goals section of
.I instrumented\-failure.log
and for the top-goal preview in diagnostics.
Both default to 4096; a nonnegative integer sets the limit, and
.B 0
or
.B unlimited
removes it.
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_CACHE_TRACE
.B 1
prints cache and pipeline trace lines.
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_TOOL_CACHE_DIR
Set by holbuild, with
.BR \-\-tool\-cache ,
for each theory's HOL processes.
.TP
.BR HOLBUILD_RUN_ROOT ", " HOLBUILD_RUN_CONTEXT ", " HOLBUILD_RUN_CONTEXT_KEY ", " HOLBUILD_RUN_SOURCE ", " HOLBUILD_RUN_OUTPUT_DIR ", " HOLBUILD_RUN_SCRATCH
Set by holbuild for a script started by
.BR run\-action .
.TP
.B HOLBUILD_EXEC_TRUSTED_HOL_REPOSITORIES
Which HOL repositories a worker running
.B exec\-action
trusts; see the remote-execution README.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR holproject.toml ", " holbuild.toml
The project manifest.
.TP
.I .holconfig.toml
Local configuration beside the manifest (remote cache, dependency paths).
.TP
.I .holbuild/
Project build outputs, logs and state.
.TP
.IR $HOLBUILD_CACHE/hol\-toolchains/
Built HOL toolchains and analysers.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, including interruption.
75 when a
.B \-\-remote\-only
build or
.B run\-action
stopped where a local build would go on.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
holbuild MyTheory
holbuild \-j4 \-\-max\-heap 4096 build MyTheory
holbuild build \-\-force=theory \-\-tactic\-timeout 10 MyTheory
holbuild check MyTheory
holbuild \-\-remote\-cache URL build \-\-remote\-exec URL MyTheory
holbuild export \-o out.hbx MyTheory
holbuild gc \-\-cache\-only \-\-retention\-days 30
.fi
.
.SH SEE ALSO
The README in the holbuild repository,
.UR https://github.com/HOL-Theorem-Prover/holbuild
.UE .
